---
id: org.dxos.plugin.deepseek
name: DeepSeekPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A **headless** Composer plugin that makes [DeepSeek](https://platform.deepseek.com)
connectable. It has no React/UI surfaces and contributes one thing: a
**Connector** entry (`source: "deepseek.com"`) with an API-key credential form,
so the user connects DeepSeek through the generic `plugin-connector` UI. On
submit the key is stored as an `AccessToken` (source `deepseek.com`) plus a
`Connection` in ECHO, resolvable later via `CredentialsService`.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                     |
| ------ | ----------------------- |
| `feat` | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0` |
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0` |
| `flow` | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0` |

## Connector

```mdl
feat DeepSeekConnector
  desc: >
    Contributes a ConnectorEntry via Capability.contribute(Connector,
    [entry]) on the connector Start activation event (mirrors
    plugin-ideogram's non-OAuth credentialForm connector).
  id: org.dxos.plugin.deepseek.connector
  source: deepseek.com
  label: DeepSeek
  credentialForm:
    schema: DeepSeekTokenForm { token: string }   # the API key, Password format
    onSubmit: >
      Trim the token; if empty, throw. Build
      Obj.make(AccessToken, { source: "deepseek.com", token }) and
      Obj.make(Connection, { name: "DeepSeek", connectorId: <id>,
      accessToken: Ref.make(accessToken) }); return
      { kind: "complete", accessToken, connection }.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Connector builds AccessToken + Connection
  given: the DeepSeek ConnectorEntry
  when: credentialForm.onSubmit runs with { token: "sk-…" }
  then:
    - returns kind "complete"
    - accessToken.source === "deepseek.com" and accessToken.token === "sk-…"
    - connection.connectorId === the entry id and references the accessToken
```

```mdl
test T-2: Empty token rejected
  given: the DeepSeek ConnectorEntry
  when: credentialForm.onSubmit runs with { token: "  " }
  then: it throws (no AccessToken / Connection created)
```

## QA

Executable flows against the running app. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where
the step maps to an invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and
step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Connect DeepSeek with an API key
  desc: >
    The whole plugin, end to end — enable it, create a Connection choosing DeepSeek, paste a key,
    and see the connection listed under the space's Connections.
  actors: human
  covers: [DeepSeekConnector, T-1, T-2]
  status: passing            # 2026-08-27; recorded against the PR preview deployment
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open (the default "My Space" is fine)
    - plugin-deepseek is OFF — it is a `labs` plugin and off by default; enabling is step 1
    - no connection named "DeepSeek" exists in that space — ABORT rather than deleting one this
      flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Enable the plugin
      do: Open Plugins from the sidebar, filter for "deep", and toggle DeepSeek on.
      expect: the DeepSeek card shows the LABS tag and its toggle reads on
      note: >
        NO `invoke` — enabling is a UI action; `manager.enable()` from the debug port does not
        perform it (same finding as plugin-chess QA-1).
    - name: Open the space's Connections panel
      do: Return to the space, expand Settings in the navtree and click Connections.
      expect: the Connections panel opens, listing no DeepSeek connection yet
    - name: Create a Connection and choose DeepSeek
      do: Click + on the space, choose Connection, pick DeepSeek in the Service dropdown, Save.
      expect: >
        DeepSeek is offered in the Service dropdown alongside the other connectors, and choosing it
        opens a "Connect DeepSeek" dialog with a single required "API key" field
      note: |
        DeepSeek appears in that dropdown only because the plugin was enabled in step 1 — the
        connector entry is contributed on the connector Start event.

        The Connections panel's own "Connect" button does NOT reach this dialog — it is inert
        (plugin-connector's `handleAdd` invokes `OpenObjectForm` with a `typename` and nothing
        opens, no error). Reproduced on a fresh profile, and unrelated to this plugin; the `+`
        path in `do:` is the working gesture. Reported, not fixed here.
    - name: Reject an empty key
      do: With the API key field left empty, click Save.
      expect: >
        no connection is created — the credential form's onSubmit refuses an all-whitespace key
        (T-2). The dialog closes without a message, which is the generic dialog's behaviour for
        every credential-form connector, not this plugin's.
    - name: Paste the API key
      do: Reopen the dialog as in step 3 and type a key into the API key field.
      expect: the field masks its input (Password format), so the key is never shown in the clear
    - name: Save the connection
      do: Click Save.
      expect: >
        a DeepSeek row appears under Settings -> Connections in the navtree and opens as its own
        plank titled "DeepSeek" (T-1 — an AccessToken with source `deepseek.com` plus a Connection
        referencing it)
  after:
    - name: Delete the connection
      do: Open the DeepSeek connection and click "Delete connection".
      expect: the row leaves the navtree, its plank closes, and a "Connection deleted" toast appears
      note: >
        NO `invoke` — the connection is created by a UI gesture in step 6, which has no operation to
        `capture` from, so there is no captured connection value for `space.removeObjects` to name.
        The delete action in the connection's own panel routes through that operation anyway.
```

## Out of scope (v1)

- Any DeepSeek API client / model provider; this version only stores the credential.
- OAuth (DeepSeek uses a static API key).
- Multi-account configuration.
